+# Read-only generation-aware monitoring repair
+
+The registry referred to an unmounted generation; logs/statistics failed ENOENT.
+The old health file was returned HEALTHY without timestamp checks, and BOT-
+prefix classification mislabeled eight renamed local bots as humans.
+
+This branch accepts a private, reviewed receipt pinning result hash, PID/start/
+CWD/UID/cgroup, binaries and profile/GUID hashes. Live telemetry must confirm the
+expected local count and recent actions; the query socket belongs to the pinned
+Dedicated PID. Name matching only associates already verified roster members;
+duplicate names are unassociated. Every slot remains identity-unknown until authoritative server-side GUID/session bindings are available. Roster associations have separate counts; no confirmed bot/human claims.
+
+Health reports current observation timestamps and explicit LIMITED coverage;
+stale source health and unverified generation/sync history are alerts. It does
+not inherit historical zero sync counters or claim native qualification. Missing
+logs produce explicit unavailable responses. Multi-packet GameSpy replies must
+be complete and from the expected loopback port.
+
+Local regressions cover spoofed names, stale/future health, missing logs,
+fragment order, PID reuse, binary changes, GUID changes, stale telemetry and
+query-socket ownership. Runtime only reads files/sockets. No game operation or
+new admin capability was added. Private receipt/registry stay outside Git.
+
+Independent review: missing-history UI and UDP address ownership findings reproduced RED then GREEN. Unique former roster nickname now stays unknown with an explicit association label, also RED then GREEN. Missing authoritative server-side GUID/session observation remains a blocker for confirmed classifications.
+
+Service preflight found EACCES on /proc/<nobody-pid>/cwd under the original
+CAP_DAC_READ_SEARCH-only sandbox. A transient service reproduced it. The
+read-only observation profile adds CAP_SYS_PTRACE, denies @debug syscalls,
+and remounts /proc read-only. Its own helper proved process-CWD read works,
+ptrace(TRACEME) returns EPERM and opening /proc/self/mem for write is denied.
+No game process memory was accessed or instrumented. Loopback-only HTTP/UDP,
+ProtectSystem, task/memory limits and no admin tools remain in force.
+
+Deployment: immutable release /srv/ssam-monitor-release-20261025-b7bda00;
+private registry/receipt/evidence /srv/tse-monitor-evidence-20261025. Existing
+source repo/dirty registry preserved. Only the app service was restarted;
+game identities and 12 binary pins rechecked unchanged. Remove only drop-in
+/etc/systemd/system/alpha-gaming-control.service.d/20261025-monitoring.conf,
+daemon-reload and restart the app to roll back. Initial connection calls during
+restart timed out; subsequent get_health returned fresh LIMITED and verified
+process/query/telemetry evidence. This is not a full historical sync monitor.
+
+Service syscall-list inspection showed @debug does not include process_vm_writev/readv on this systemd version. Those calls and process_madvise are now explicitly denied. An owned transient helper proved both zero-vector process_vm calls return EPERM. No target game memory was accessed.
